window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-7967b4bf527099cb"]={"key":"ny_main-7967b4bf527099cb","group":"ny_main","uid":"7967b4bf527099cb","rank":19,"title":"england damp mould scope board control normative 01","occupation":"lawyers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the lawyer supporting Cavendish Manufacturing’s board on its England housing obligations, working with Candlewick Energy as the property-services contractor. Sasha Wainwright needs a neutral board briefing and publication-control record before the board meeting on 19 June 2026. Callum Rivenburgh has identified that the completed evidence bundle can support two reasonable readings of “affected homes”: every home in an identified block, or only homes with recorded damp-and-mould reports. The evidence bundle is not supplied with this request, so do not manufacture household facts, addresses, report counts, inspection records, cost rates, tenant names, legal citations, thresholds, or a tenant-notice duration. Where a figure or proposition cannot be substantiated from material actually available to you, use the exact status `NOT ESTABLISHED`, say what source or owner is needed, and show the calculation basis rather than treating the gap as zero. Produce exactly one file, `cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx`, in the top level of the working directory where you start. Combine the board-facing briefing and the publication-control workbook in that one XLSX; do not create a second document. The workbook must contain clearly identified sections or sheets named exactly `Board Briefing`, `Scope Comparison`, `Publication Control`, and `Assumptions & Gaps`. Keep the board-facing briefing to no more than 700 words and no more than ten numbered decision points. It is for legally experienced executives and operational board members, so make it concise and decision-ready rather than a legal tutorial. 1) State that the document is accurate as at 12 June 2026 and use the exact shared labels `BLOCK-SCOPE` and `REPORT-SCOPE` throughout. Define what each reading treats as an affected home, while keeping the two readings separate rather than blending them. 2) For each reading, set out the home, inspection, and cost figures for two clearly labelled periods, `PRIOR PERIOD` and `PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026`; define the date boundaries you use, identify material changes, and explain why a change matters. Use `NOT ESTABLISHED` where the absent bundle prevents a supported number, with a formula or counting rule and the missing evidence owner beside it. 3) Distinguish what the governing damp-and-mould standard requires from what the Cavendish Manufacturing policy promises, and do not present the broader interpretation as legally compelled merely because it may be operationally prudent. Do not state a legal threshold or citation unless it is accurate and its applicability is clear. 4) Address the collision between the policy’s tenant-notice period and work needed immediately to control a serious hazard. Show the issue without silently selecting a result, preserve the difference between urgent hazard control and routine planned access, and identify the record, owner, and communication needed when the normal notice path cannot be followed. Do not invent the notice period. 5) Sasha is concerned that a block-wide reading could be misused as proof that every home has an individually confirmed hazard. Actively discourage that misuse in prominent board language, and make clear what further operational verification is needed before household-level action. 6) Mark the boundary between legal interpretation and Candlewick Energy’s operational inspection, resident-contact, remedial-work, and costing responsibilities; do not perform or imply a survey or approve a cost estimate that the evidence does not support. 7) Use the publication-control section to record the current draft, the proposed publication state, the board-approval gate, the person responsible for each unresolved input, timing before publication, and a concise change log showing what the authorized action changes. End with a neutral statement of the decision the board must make or the information it must withhold approval for, not a recommendation for either reading and not a generic list of future steps. Minimize sensitive household information: use no names, addresses, or identifying case details, and ensure every label and figure shown in the briefing agrees with the corresponding control tables.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx` — A single combined XLSX containing a concise neutral board briefing and a publication-control workbook for the two affected-home interpretations. (Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly this filename.; Include clearly identified sections or sheets named exactly Board Briefing, Scope Comparison, Publication Control, and Assumptions & Gaps.; Keep the board-facing briefing to no more than 700 words and no more than ten numbered decision points.; Use the exact shared labels BLOCK-SCOPE, REPORT-SCOPE, PRIOR PERIOD, PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026, and NOT ESTABLISHED where applicable.; Do not include household names, addresses, or other identifying details.; Do not create a second deliverable, use external links, or rely on unsupported invented facts.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx","bytes":22362,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/4beab31472f291c6a6c38c083a61799e6faf6e845c79a2e6f339b95f9eeeba4a.xlsx","sha256":"4beab31472f291c6a6c38c083a61799e6faf6e845c79a2e6f339b95f9eeeba4a","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Board Briefing","row_count":20,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Cavendish Manufacturing | England housing obligations"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Damp-and-mould scope and publication control | Board Briefing"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Accurate as at 12 June 2026"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Prepared for","Sasha Wainwright","","","Board meeting","19 June 2026"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Current draft","DRAFT v0.1 - NOT APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION","","","Evidence position","No evidence bundle supplied"]},{"r":"8","cells":["BOARD CONTROL - DO NOT USE BLOCK-SCOPE AS PROOF THAT EVERY INDIVIDUAL HOME HAS A CONFIRMED DAMP-AND-MOULD HAZARD.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Before household-level action, Candlewick Energy must complete appropriate home-level operational verification. A block-level count is not a substitute; no household-level fact is established by this pack.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["DECISION POINTS | BOARD-FACING BRIEFING"]},{"r":"12","cells":["No.","Decision point","","","","","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["1","Two readings remain live. BLOCK-SCOPE treats each home in an identified block as affected, whether or not that home has a recorded damp-and-mould report. REPORT-SCOPE treats only each unique home with a recorded damp-and-mould report in the defined period as affected. They are separate readings; this pack does not select one.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["2","Evidence status. For both readings, homes, inspections and cost exposure are NOT ESTABLISHED for PRIOR PERIOD and PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026. The completed evidence bundle is unavailable. No household fact, address, report count, inspection record, cost rate or zero is inferred; Candlewick Energy owns the operational bundle and Cavendish Finance owns rate inputs.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["3","Period boundaries. PRIOR PERIOD is 1 June 2025 to 31 May 2026, inclusive. PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026 is 1 June 2026 to 12 June 2026, inclusive. These are control boundaries pending confirmation against the bundle reporting calendar; the dates do not imply that activity occurred.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["4","Material change. Direction, magnitude and cause of change in scope population, inspection demand or cost exposure are NOT ESTABLISHED. Candlewick Energy must reconcile the identified-block register, unique report-home log, inspection records and work orders by period. Without that evidence, no increase, decrease or causal explanation can support publication.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["5","Cost basis. Cost exposure is NOT ESTABLISHED under either reading. The controlled calculation is SUM(validated quantity by work type x validated rate) plus validated materials, access, reinspection and other documented ancillary components, with the population and period stated. Candlewick Energy and Cavendish Finance own those inputs; Legal does not approve absent rates.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["6","Legal versus policy. The governing damp-and-mould standard is an external requirement; the Cavendish Manufacturing policy is an internal promise and control, and may be more demanding. Cavendish Legal must verify the relevant legal source, threshold, citation and applicability; each is NOT ESTABLISHED here. A broader operational reading is not legally compelled merely because it is prudent or promised by policy.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["7","Notice and urgency. The policy's normal tenant-notice duration is NOT ESTABLISHED. Routine planned access follows the approved notice path. Work needed immediately to control a serious hazard is a separate, fact-sensitive control path: normal notice is not treated as an absolute precondition to necessary urgent control, but neither is notice silently waived. Candlewick Energy records the reason, owner, decision, action and access record, then provides resident communication and follow-up; Legal reviews the applicable basis.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["8","Boundary and gate. Legal interprets the alternatives and control wording. Candlewick Energy owns operational inspection, resident contact and remedial-work decisions; Candlewick Energy and Cavendish Finance own costing. The current draft is DRAFT v0.1, and the proposed publication state is HOLD pending board approval and closure or explicit treatment of gaps. The board must decide whether to approve a specified neutral publication state or withhold approval; this pack recommends neither BLOCK-SCOPE nor REPORT-SCOPE.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["BOARD DECISION / APPROVAL CONDITION"]},{"r":"23","cells":["The board must either record the publication wording and control state for both readings, without presenting BLOCK-SCOPE as individual confirmation, or withhold publication approval until the identified evidence, legal/policy inputs, urgent-control record and costing basis are resolved or expressly accepted as NOT ESTABLISHED. No reading is recommended here.","","","","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Briefing control check: 459 words in numbered narrative | 8 numbered decision points | all unsupported operational figures remain NOT ESTABLISHED."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Scope Comparison","row_count":25,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Scope Comparison | Two controlled readings"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Homes, inspections and cost exposure by period | no evidence bundle supplied"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Accurate as at 12 June 2026"]},{"r":"5","cells":["EVIDENCE STATUS: every comparison value below is NOT ESTABLISHED. This is a controlled absence of support, not zero. The corresponding source, owner and calculation basis are stated beside each status.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["PERIOD BOUNDARIES"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Period label","Inclusive date boundary","Control use","","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["PRIOR PERIOD","1 June 2025 to 31 May 2026 (inclusive)","Comparison baseline; confirm the bundle reporting calendar before populating any status.","","","",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026","1 June 2026 to 12 June 2026 (inclusive)","Current cut-off used by this pack; no activity is implied by the boundary.","","","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["INTERPRETATION COMPARISON"]},{"r":"14","cells":["BLOCK-SCOPE","","","","","",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["Affected home definition: each home in an identified block is treated as affected, whether or not an individual damp-and-mould report is recorded.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["Metric / unit","Scope status","PRIOR PERIOD","PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026","Material change / why it matters","Counting or calculation basis","Missing evidence / owner"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Homes\nunique homes","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: no period-over-period direction or magnitude can be established; the population choice changes publication wording and household verification burden.","Count unique home keys in the identified-block register for each period; deduplicate a home once within an identified block and reconcile block status at period end.","Completed evidence bundle: identified-block register, period fields and duplicate rule. Owner: Candlewick Energy operational data lead."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Inspections\ninspection records / visits","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: a change in inspection demand cannot be inferred from a home count; it matters to access capacity and verification coverage.","Count completed and attempted inspection records by event date and scope; retain the visit/record unit and link to the relevant home key. Do not equate homes with inspections.","Inspection and job records with period status. Owner: Candlewick Energy inspection lead."]},{"r":"19","cells":["Cost exposure\nvalidated GBP exposure","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: no supported change in exposure; it matters to approval, reserves and the publication of any financial figure.","SUM(validated quantity by work type x validated rate) + validated materials, access, reinspection and other documented ancillary costs; state population and period; no unsupported rate.","Work orders, scope quantities, approved rate card and finance validation. Owners: Candlewick Energy commercial lead and Cavendish Finance."]},{"r":"21","cells":["REPORT-SCOPE","","","","","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["Affected home definition: only each unique home with a recorded damp-and-mould report in the defined period is treated as affected.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["Metric / unit","Scope status","PRIOR PERIOD","PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026","Material change / why it matters","Counting or calculation basis","Missing evidence / owner"]},{"r":"24","cells":["Homes\nunique homes","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: no period-over-period direction or magnitude can be established; the population may differ from BLOCK-SCOPE and affects household verification.","Count unique homes with a recorded damp-and-mould report in each period; deduplicate multiple reports for one home for the home count, while retaining report events separately.","Completed evidence bundle: report log, stable home key, report date and duplicate rule. Owner: Candlewick Energy resident-contact/data lead."]},{"r":"25","cells":["Inspections\ninspection records / visits","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: reports cannot be treated as inspections; change matters to verification, access demand and response control.","Count completed and attempted inspection records/visits linked to reporting homes by event date; retain report-to-inspection linkage and do not infer unreported homes.","Inspection/job records and report linkage. Owner: Candlewick Energy inspection lead."]},{"r":"26","cells":["Cost exposure\nvalidated GBP exposure","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED","NOT ESTABLISHED: no supported change in exposure; it matters to the financial consequence of publishing the narrower reading.","SUM(validated quantity by work type x validated rate) + validated materials, access, reinspection and other documented ancillary costs for unique reporting homes; state allocation rule and period.","Work orders, report linkage, validated quantities/rates and finance review. Owners: Candlewick Energy commercial lead and Cavendish Finance."]},{"r":"28","cells":["BOARD CONTROL | HOUSEHOLD VERIFICATION"]},{"r":"29","cells":["DO NOT USE BLOCK-SCOPE AS PROOF THAT EVERY INDIVIDUAL HOME HAS A CONFIRMED DAMP-AND-MOULD HAZARD. Before household-level action, Candlewick Energy must complete appropriate operational verification; the block-level count is not a substitute.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["LEGAL / OPERATIONAL BOUNDARY"]},{"r":"32","cells":["Legal interprets the two readings and controls publication wording. Candlewick Energy owns operational inspection, resident contact, remedial-work decisions, work-order evidence and household verification. Candlewick Energy and Cavendish Finance own quantities, rates and costing. This sheet performs no survey and approves no unsupported estimate.","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Publication Control","row_count":27,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Publication Control | Board approval record"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Current draft, proposed state, unresolved inputs and authorized changes"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Accurate as at 12 June 2026"]},{"r":"5","cells":["PUBLICATION STATE"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Document status","CURRENT DRAFT: DRAFT v0.1 - NOT APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION","","","","Prepared by Sasha Wainwright; controlled briefing only.",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["Proposed publication state","HOLD - BOARD APPROVAL REQUIRED BEFORE PUBLICATION","","","","No release until the gate and unresolved-input controls below are recorded.",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["Board approval gate","Board decision recorded in minutes at the 19 June 2026 meeting","","","","The gate is mandatory before publication; this workbook does not record a decision.",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Timing before publication","Publication date NOT ESTABLISHED","","","","Sasha Wainwright / Board Secretary confirms timing only after approval and required sign-offs.",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["URGENT HAZARD CONTROL | NOTICE EXCEPTION RECORD"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Normal tenant-notice duration: NOT ESTABLISHED. If work is needed immediately to control a serious hazard and the normal notice path cannot be followed, Candlewick Energy's operational lead must record the reason, urgency, decision-maker, action, time and access/work-order record; the resident-contact lead must provide communication and follow-up; Cavendish Legal reviews the applicable basis. Routine planned access remains on the normal notice path. This control does not silently select a legal result.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["UNRESOLVED INPUTS AND CONTROL ACTIONS"]},{"r":"15","cells":["ID","Input / decision / control","Status","Responsible owner","Required source or record","Timing / gate","Effect on publication"]},{"r":"16","cells":["PC-01","Scope wording and board decision","NOT ESTABLISHED","Board; Board Secretary","Minutes recording whether and how BLOCK-SCOPE and REPORT-SCOPE are approved; this draft makes no selection.","At 19 June 2026 board meeting; mandatory before publication.","No approved scope wording until the gate is recorded."]},{"r":"17","cells":["PC-02","Completed evidence bundle and period reconciliation","NOT ESTABLISHED","Candlewick Energy operational data lead","Identified-block register, report log, inspection/job records, work orders, reporting calendar and duplicate rules.","Before approval of any number, or before any number is published.","Replace NOT ESTABLISHED only with traceable status and retained counting basis."]},{"r":"18","cells":["PC-03","External damp-and-mould standard: proposition and applicability","NOT ESTABLISHED","Cavendish Legal","Current applicable legal/regulatory source, tenancy/access context and verified facts; cite only after proposition and applicability are checked.","Legal sign-off before publication.","No threshold, citation or statement that BLOCK-SCOPE is legally compelled."]},{"r":"19","cells":["PC-04","Cavendish policy version and normal tenant-notice period","NOT ESTABLISHED","Cavendish Housing Policy owner","Approved policy version and exact notice wording/duration; duration is currently NOT ESTABLISHED.","Before board approval of notice wording and before publication.","Keep routine access and urgent control paths distinct; do not invent a duration."]},{"r":"20","cells":["PC-05","Urgent serious-hazard control where normal notice path cannot be followed","NOT ESTABLISHED","Candlewick Energy operational lead; Cavendish Legal","Contemporaneous incident/inspection/access record: reason, urgency, decision-maker, action, time, work order and applicable legal/policy basis.","At the event; review before closure and before publication of the exception control.","Retain a conditional, auditable exception; do not treat urgent control as routine access."]},{"r":"21","cells":["PC-06","Resident communication and follow-up after urgent action","NOT ESTABLISHED","Candlewick Energy resident-contact lead","Approved communication record, contact attempt/outcome, explanation of action and follow-up access/repair arrangement.","Promptly after urgent action and before case closure; control checked before release.","No notice-exception wording released without a communication trail."]},{"r":"22","cells":["PC-07","Household-level verification before household action","NOT ESTABLISHED","Candlewick Energy inspection lead","Home-level inspection/verification records and decision trail; a block-level count is not evidence of an individual confirmed hazard.","Before any household-level action.","BLOCK-SCOPE warning must remain prominent; no block count substitution."]},{"r":"23","cells":["PC-08","Cost quantities, rates and allocation by scope and period","NOT ESTABLISHED","Candlewick Energy commercial lead; Cavendish Finance","Validated work types, quantities, approved rates, materials, access, reinspection and other ancillary inputs, with scope allocation.","Before any cost figure or estimate is published or approved.","Legal analysis does not validate absent rates; unsupported exposure remains NOT ESTABLISHED."]},{"r":"24","cells":["PC-09","Release authorization and version record","NOT ESTABLISHED","Sasha Wainwright; Board Secretary","Approved version, board minutes, legal sign-off, operational evidence sign-off and final change log.","After the 19 June 2026 gate; publication date NOT ESTABLISHED until recorded.","Current draft remains HOLD until the approval condition is met."]},{"r":"26","cells":["AUTHORIZED CHANGE LOG"]},{"r":"27","cells":["Date","Version / status","Authorized action","Scope wording change","Control wording / status change","Owner","Gate / timing"]},{"r":"28","cells":["12 June 2026","DRAFT v0.1","Prepare controlled board pack","Added separate BLOCK-SCOPE and REPORT-SCOPE definitions; no interpretation selected.","Added prominent block-level misuse warning, NOT ESTABLISHED statuses, period boundaries and notice/urgency control.","Sasha Wainwright","Before 19 June 2026 board meeting."]},{"r":"29","cells":["19 June 2026","PROPOSED v1.0 / HOLD","Board records approval decision","Only wording recorded in the minutes may change the publication scope state; both labels remain traceable.","Update board-approval gate, owner sign-off and change status; do not populate unsupported figures.","Board / Board Secretary","Approval gate before publication."]},{"r":"30","cells":["After gate","RELEASE CANDIDATE","Release only after approved inputs","Replace only validated NOT ESTABLISHED statuses; retain selected label, period and calculation basis.","Update version, evidence trail, urgent-control wording and communication control as applicable.","Sasha Wainwright / control owners","Publication date NOT ESTABLISHED until recorded."]},{"r":"32","cells":["STATUS RULE: NOT ESTABLISHED means the supplied material does not support the input. It is not zero, not an approval, and not a finding about any individual home.","","","","","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Assumptions & Gaps","row_count":21,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Assumptions & Gaps | Evidence and ownership register"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Closed-world control record | no supplied reference files"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Accurate as at 12 June 2026"]},{"r":"5","cells":["EVIDENCE BOUNDARY: no evidence bundle or other reference file was supplied. This register records what is missing and who must resolve it; NOT ESTABLISHED is a controlled status, never a zero or an implied household fact.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["CONTROLLED ASSUMPTIONS AND EVIDENCE GAPS"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Gap ID","Topic","Status","Missing evidence / input","Calculation or control basis","Responsible owner / source","Timing / publication consequence"]},{"r":"9","cells":["AG-01","Evidence bundle availability","NOT ESTABLISHED","The completed evidence bundle is absent from the supplied material.","No homes, inspections, costs, report counts, addresses or household facts may be inferred; retain the source package and version used.","Candlewick Energy operational data lead / completed evidence bundle.","Before board approval or publication; all dependent fields stay NOT ESTABLISHED."]},{"r":"10","cells":["AG-02","BLOCK-SCOPE population","NOT ESTABLISHED","Identified-block register, period status and stable internal home key are missing.","Home figure = unique homes in identified blocks for the period, deduplicated within block; block membership must be evidenced.","Candlewick Energy operational data lead / block register and data dictionary.","Before BLOCK-SCOPE wording or household action is approved."]},{"r":"11","cells":["AG-03","REPORT-SCOPE population","NOT ESTABLISHED","Dated damp-and-mould report log, stable home key and report deduplication rule are missing.","Home figure = unique reporting homes by period; multiple reports for one home are retained as events but counted once for homes.","Candlewick Energy resident-contact/data lead / report log.","Before REPORT-SCOPE wording or any report-based figure is published."]},{"r":"12","cells":["AG-04","Inspection unit and demand","NOT ESTABLISHED","Completed/attempted inspection records, event dates and linkage to scope populations are missing.","Inspection figure counts inspection records/visits, not homes or reports; compare by event date and preserve the unit.","Candlewick Energy inspection lead / inspection and job records.","Before describing material inspection change or operational capacity."]},{"r":"13","cells":["AG-05","Cost exposure and rates","NOT ESTABLISHED","Validated quantities, work types, rate card, materials, access, reinspection and other ancillary inputs are missing.","Cost = SUM(validated quantity by work type x validated rate) + validated documented ancillary components, allocated to scope and period; no unsupported rate.","Candlewick Energy commercial lead + Cavendish Finance / work orders and rate validation.","Before any cost figure, reserve implication or estimate is approved."]},{"r":"14","cells":["AG-06","Period calendar","NOT ESTABLISHED","The bundle reporting calendar and event-date convention are missing.","Working control boundaries are PRIOR PERIOD: 1 June 2025 to 31 May 2026 inclusive; PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026: 1 June 2026 to 12 June 2026 inclusive. Confirm before calculation.","Candlewick Energy data owner + Board Secretary / bundle metadata.","Before period comparison is treated as material or published."]},{"r":"15","cells":["AG-07","Governing damp-and-mould standard","NOT ESTABLISHED","The current legal/regulatory source, proposition and applicability to the relevant housing and tenancy facts are not supplied.","Legal must verify the exact external requirement before any threshold, citation or mandate wording is used; no legal threshold is asserted here.","Cavendish Legal / current applicable source and verified facts.","Legal sign-off is a pre-publication gate."]},{"r":"16","cells":["AG-08","Cavendish policy and tenant notice","NOT ESTABLISHED","Approved policy version and exact normal tenant-notice wording/duration are missing.","Policy promises are internal controls and may be more demanding than an external minimum; normal notice duration remains NOT ESTABLISHED.","Cavendish Housing Policy owner / approved policy record.","Before notice wording or routine access control is approved."]},{"r":"17","cells":["AG-09","Urgent serious-hazard action","NOT ESTABLISHED","No incident/inspection/access record is supplied for a case where the normal notice path cannot be followed.","Urgent hazard control and routine planned access are separate paths. Record reason, urgency, decision-maker, action, time, access/work order and applicable basis; do not silently waive notice.","Candlewick Energy operational lead; Cavendish Legal / incident, access and work-order record.","Record at event; review before closure and before exception wording is published."]},{"r":"18","cells":["AG-10","Household-level verification","NOT ESTABLISHED","Home-level inspection/verification records and decision trail are missing.","BLOCK-SCOPE classification is not proof that every individual home has a confirmed damp-and-mould hazard; appropriate operational verification is required before household-level action.","Candlewick Energy inspection lead / home-level records.","Before any household-level contact, remedial-work decision or action."]},{"r":"19","cells":["AG-11","Resident communication and follow-up","NOT ESTABLISHED","Approved resident-contact record, contact outcome and follow-up access/repair communication are missing.","After urgent action, provide and retain the required communication and follow-up; do not treat the absence of a notice record as the end of the control.","Candlewick Energy resident-contact lead / contact and communication record.","Promptly after urgent action; before case closure and publication sign-off."]},{"r":"20","cells":["AG-12","Board approval and release record","NOT ESTABLISHED","Board minutes, approved version and final legal/operational sign-offs are not yet available.","Current draft is DRAFT v0.1; proposed state is HOLD. Release only after the 19 June 2026 board gate and recorded treatment of gaps.","Board / Board Secretary; Sasha Wainwright coordinates release record.","Mandatory pre-publication gate; publication date NOT ESTABLISHED."]},{"r":"22","cells":["OWNERSHIP BOUNDARY"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Legal interprets the alternatives, checks the applicable external standard and controls publication wording. Legal does not inspect homes, contact residents, choose remedial work, set operational rates or approve an unsupported cost estimate. Candlewick Energy owns inspection, resident contact, remedial-work decisions and operational evidence; Cavendish Finance validates costing inputs.","","","","","",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Privacy control: no household names, addresses or identifying case details are included. Any operational source used later must be minimised before it is attached to a publication record."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is an XLSX file with the exact required filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"File name and MIME/type inspection.","grader_hint":"Confirm that exactly one submitted file is named cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx and opens as an XLSX workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains the four required named sections or sheets: Board Briefing, Scope Comparison, Publication Control, and Assumptions & Gaps.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook sheet names or clearly labelled section headings.","grader_hint":"Inspect workbook structure and accept a section within a sheet only if it is unambiguous and named exactly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The board-facing briefing is no more than 700 words and contains no more than ten numbered decision points.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered Board Briefing text.","grader_hint":"Count words in the board-facing narrative and count numbered points; exclude table labels and source notes from the word count only when clearly separated from the briefing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact states that it is accurate as at 12 June 2026.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Board Briefing and/or control metadata.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit as-at date, not merely a file creation date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The exact labels BLOCK-SCOPE and REPORT-SCOPE are used consistently.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Briefing and comparison tables.","grader_hint":"Check exact spelling and capitalization in both the narrative and the control tables."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"BLOCK-SCOPE is defined as treating homes in an identified block as affected, while REPORT-SCOPE is defined as treating only homes with recorded damp-and-mould reports as affected.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Definitions in the briefing or comparison section.","grader_hint":"The two definitions must remain distinct and must not be described as interchangeable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each interpretation has a separate home figure or an explicit NOT ESTABLISHED status, with a stated counting basis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope Comparison table and assumptions register.","grader_hint":"Accept a supported number only if its population and duplicate treatment are stated; otherwise require NOT ESTABLISHED plus the missing evidence and formula."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each interpretation has a separate inspection figure or NOT ESTABLISHED status, and the artifact distinguishes homes from inspections.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope Comparison table.","grader_hint":"Do not award this for repeating the home count as an inspection count without explaining the inspection unit and basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each interpretation has a separate cost figure or NOT ESTABLISHED status, with cost components or a transparent calculation basis.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope Comparison and Assumptions & Gaps.","grader_hint":"A cost figure must identify what it covers and its rate or source; unsupported rates must be marked NOT ESTABLISHED rather than invented."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact uses the exact period labels PRIOR PERIOD and PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Period comparison headings.","grader_hint":"Require both exact labels and do not accept only generic words such as previous and current."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The date boundaries for both comparison periods are explicitly stated.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Period definitions or notes.","grader_hint":"The periods must be reproducible and must not overlap ambiguously."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material changes are identified separately for scope, inspection demand, cost exposure, or publication control, rather than merely listing two columns.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Briefing analysis and comparison section.","grader_hint":"Award only where the artifact explains which change is material and what decision or control consequence follows."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact explains the reason or evidential basis for each claimed material change, and marks the change NOT ESTABLISHED when that basis is unavailable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Narrative analysis and assumptions register.","grader_hint":"Do not award for unsupported causal language or for treating missing data as evidence of no change."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The governing damp-and-mould standard is distinguished from the promises and internal controls of the Cavendish Manufacturing policy.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Legal analysis in Board Briefing.","grader_hint":"Look for separate treatment of external requirement and internal policy commitment, including the consequence of a policy being more demanding than a minimum standard."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact does not present BLOCK-SCOPE as legally compelled solely because it is broader or operationally prudent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Interpretation analysis.","grader_hint":"The document may describe the risk or benefit of the broader reading, but must preserve the distinction between legal requirement and policy choice."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Unsupported legal citations, statutory thresholds, regulatory thresholds, and notice durations are either omitted or explicitly marked NOT ESTABLISHED with the required verification source.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Briefing, assumptions, and gap register.","grader_hint":"Inspect for invented precision. A citation may receive credit only if its proposition and applicability are accurately stated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The tenant-notice issue is described as a conflict between the policy's normal notice period and work needed immediately to control a serious hazard.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Board Briefing and Publication Control.","grader_hint":"The edge case must be explicit, not buried as a generic access or communications note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact keeps urgent hazard control distinct from routine planned access and does not state that normal notice is an absolute precondition to necessary urgent action.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Notice-versus-urgency analysis.","grader_hint":"Look for conditional, risk-sensitive language that avoids both an unconditional waiver of notice and an unsafe requirement to wait."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The control for a notice exception identifies the reason, responsible owner, record to retain, and communication or follow-up required after the urgent action.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Publication Control and Assumptions & Gaps.","grader_hint":"All four elements must be present; a generic instruction to document the event is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact prominently and actively warns that a block-wide classification is not proof that every individual home has a confirmed damp-and-mould hazard.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Prominent warning in Board Briefing or control section.","grader_hint":"The warning must be directive, such as a clear do-not-use statement, rather than a neutral description of possible misuse."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact states that household-level action requires appropriate operational verification and does not use the block-level count as a substitute for that verification.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope analysis and operational boundary note.","grader_hint":"Accept a clear statement of the verification dependency without requiring a detailed operational procedure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The boundary between legal interpretation and operational inspection, resident contact, and remedial-work decisions is explicitly marked.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Ownership or boundary section.","grader_hint":"The legal author must not imply that legal analysis itself confirms a physical condition or authorizes a survey outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The boundary between legal interpretation and costing or rate-setting is explicitly marked, with unsupported cost inputs assigned to an operational or finance owner.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Cost basis and ownership notes.","grader_hint":"Look for a named functional owner or role and a clear statement that legal analysis does not validate absent rates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook uses NOT ESTABLISHED instead of zero or an invented number wherever the unavailable evidence bundle prevents substantiation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"All numeric comparison and control fields.","grader_hint":"Check homes, inspections, costs, notice duration, and period changes for false precision or silent zeros."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every NOT ESTABLISHED item identifies the missing evidence or input and a responsible owner or source needed to resolve it.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Assumptions & Gaps and control register.","grader_hint":"A bare placeholder without an actionable evidence owner does not satisfy this criterion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The publication-control record states that board approval is a gate before publication and distinguishes the current draft from the proposed publication state.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Publication Control section.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit pre-publication status logic, not just a general mention of board approval."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The publication-control record documents what the authorized action changes, including version or status, scope wording, and any control wording affected.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Change log.","grader_hint":"The change log must identify changed content or control state, not merely say revised policy prepared."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each unresolved publication input has a concrete owner and timing or gate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Publication Control and Assumptions & Gaps.","grader_hint":"Accept a named person or clearly identified function and a date, meeting, or approval dependency."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing and comparison/control tables agree on both interpretation labels and every populated or NOT ESTABLISHED home, inspection, and cost status.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Internal cross-check within the single workbook.","grader_hint":"Compare narrative summaries against the corresponding table cells; discrepancies in scope labels or figures fail this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact preserves neutrality by presenting the two readings, their implications, and unresolved evidence without recommending BLOCK-SCOPE or REPORT-SCOPE.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Board Briefing conclusion.","grader_hint":"The document may identify risks and decision consequences but must not choose one interpretation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The closing statement identifies the board decision or approval condition without ending as a generic list of next steps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Final paragraph or decision box.","grader_hint":"Require a clear decision or withholding condition and no open-ended procedural conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No household names, addresses, or identifying case details appear in the workbook.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Workbook-wide privacy inspection.","grader_hint":"Synthetic role names used for governance ownership are acceptable; household-level identifiers are not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The board-facing material is concise, legible, and usable by both legally experienced executives and operational board members without becoming a tutorial.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered workbook review.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a board member can understand the two readings, the evidence limits, the urgency collision, and the approval control without asking the author to decode the artifact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is operationally usable as a publication-control record, with clear statuses, owners, evidence gaps, and change information rather than merely a prose memo placed in spreadsheet cells.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and cell structure.","grader_hint":"Judge whether an internal reviewer could locate the control state, gap owner, and change record quickly and reliably."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is an internal legal board pack for a housing-policy publication decision where the underlying evidence bundle is unavailable to the drafter. The work must preserve legally defensible alternatives while giving operational and governance owners a controlled, usable record.","difficulty_sources":["Preserving two reasonable scope readings without collapsing them into a recommendation","Reconciling legal-standard language with internal policy promises without unsupported legal claims","Handling absent evidence through transparent NOT ESTABLISHED controls rather than fabricated figures","Separating legal interpretation from operational inspection, resident contact, remedial work, and costing","Making the notice-versus-immediate-hazard collision explicit and operationally controlled","Maintaining exact labels, statuses, and figures across the briefing and workbook sections"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_files":{"count":0,"construction":"Do not construct or attach reference files. The absence of the evidence bundle is intentional and must be visible as a controlled evidence gap in a strong solution."},"gold_definition":{"overall":"A strong solution is a single combined XLSX that gives the board a neutral, concise comparison of BLOCK-SCOPE and REPORT-SCOPE, refuses unsupported factual precision, and records the publication gate and ownership boundaries.","required_content":["Use the exact labels BLOCK-SCOPE, REPORT-SCOPE, PRIOR PERIOD, PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026, and NOT ESTABLISHED.","Define both affected-home interpretations separately.","For homes, inspections, and costs, either provide supported figures with counting/calculation bases or use NOT ESTABLISHED and identify the missing evidence and owner.","Compare two explicitly bounded periods and explain material changes or explicitly state that the change is NOT ESTABLISHED.","Separate external governing requirements from Cavendish Manufacturing policy promises and avoid presenting a broader policy choice as a legal mandate.","Explain the tenant-notice versus immediate-hazard collision without choosing a hidden result; include reason, record, owner, and follow-up communication controls.","Actively warn against treating a block-wide designation as proof of an individual household hazard.","Mark legal, operational inspection, resident-contact, remedial-work, and costing boundaries.","Record current draft, proposed publication state, board approval gate, unresolved inputs, owners, timing, and an authorized change log.","Keep the conclusion neutral and decision-oriented, with no recommendation for either interpretation."],"data_integrity_rules":["Never convert missing evidence into zero.","Never invent household facts, addresses, counts, cost rates, statutory thresholds, citations, or notice durations.","Every populated figure must be traceable to a stated source or formula; because no source is supplied, the expected safe state for unsupported figures is NOT ESTABLISHED.","The briefing and control tables must use identical labels and statuses."]},"review_method":"Build an imagined reference answer offline using only occupational legal and governance knowledge. Verify the word and point caps, inspect every comparison field for unsupported precision, trace all NOT ESTABLISHED entries to an owner and missing source, compare the briefing against the control tables, and render the XLSX to confirm that both legal and operational readers can use it."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"combined_board_briefing_control_workbook","filename":"cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A single combined XLSX containing a concise neutral board briefing and a publication-control workbook for the two affected-home interpretations.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the solver's starting working directory using exactly this filename.","Include clearly identified sections or sheets named exactly Board Briefing, Scope Comparison, Publication Control, and Assumptions & Gaps.","Keep the board-facing briefing to no more than 700 words and no more than ten numbered decision points.","Use the exact shared labels BLOCK-SCOPE, REPORT-SCOPE, PRIOR PERIOD, PERIOD TO 12 JUNE 2026, and NOT ESTABLISHED where applicable.","Do not include household names, addresses, or other identifying details.","Do not create a second deliverable, use external links, or rely on unsupported invented facts."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"lawyers","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Use one legal-domain reviewer and one independent document-quality reviewer. Review the workbook from the submitted artifact alone, checking both legal defensibility and practical board usability. No external source retrieval is required or permitted; unsupported factual precision should be treated as a defect, while explicit NOT ESTABLISHED statuses with owners and calculation bases are acceptable.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Because no evidence bundle is supplied, there is no single correct numeric answer for homes, inspections, costs, or notice duration.","The gold standard is therefore relational and control-based: it rewards transparent non-invention, distinct interpretations, and reproducible calculation bases.","Exact legal citations are not required; any citation used must be accurate and applicable."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:01:51+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:01:51+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:01:51+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:01:51+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/7967b4bf527099cb","declared_deliverables":["cavendish_damp_mould_board_control.xlsx"]};
